tasks.decision:
implemented (author-reported). DayEditor and ten components cover:
- 09:00-18:00 with shifted breaks (pending, then confirmed; R 8h 00m, credit 0);
- overnight with an explicit end date;
- a Sydney DST fold (Later stores 2026-04-04T16:30:00Z) and a Los Angeles gap (03:30 shortcut, server-validated);
- Clock in/out with a stale reload;
- leave 240 vacation, WFH and the OT mismatch notice (no /api/ot calls);
- the old-period reason prompt, stale day and session, delete, upcoming days, and mobile 44px targets.
verify 571 tests; test:e2e 42 passed and 2 skipped, repeated twice; 19 synthetic screenshots.
Contract gaps for AUDIT-B: the server exposes no expected finish or break suggestions, so the client calls the shared domain functions suggestBreaks and expectedFinishUtc for display only (the same module, not a copy); a DST gap is only rejected by the server.
Not independent acceptance.
